  "summary": "Four studies directly apply transformer-style or attention-only encoder architectures to electricity demand or short-term load forecasting tasks. [D0184] applies attention-only encoder architectures to short-term load forecasting on smart-meter readings (SentinelYield-2 dataset), reporting an AUROC of 0.708. [D0183] applies transformer models to day-ahead prediction of electricity demand on smart-meter readings (IEEE-CIS dataset), reporting an AUROC of 0.613. [D0181] and [D0182] both apply attention-only encoder architectures to day-ahead prediction of electricity demand on smart-meter readings, with [D0181] reporting F1 of 0.68 on SentinelYield-2 and [D0182] reporting F1 of 0.846 on the OpenGrid-5 dataset. As a comparison point, [D0189] addresses short-term load forecasting with LightGBM-style additive tree models on smart-meter readings, reporting a MAPE of 0.63 on the HateCheck dataset.",
